  "wikitext": "{{Stub|Profile needs updating}}\n{{CustomTabs\n|subpages=0\n|tab1=Fenrico\n|tab1name=Overview\n|tab2=Fenrico/Boss\n|tab2name=Boss\n|tab3=Reminiscence: Fenrico\n|tab3name=Echo}}\n{{NPC Infobox\n|image            = NPC Fenrico.png\n|type             = Resonator\n|type2            = Quest\n|realname         = Fenrico Macbeth\n|nation           = Rinascita\n|location         = Cathedral of Mercury\n|affiliation      = Order of the Deep\n|affiliation2     = \n|title            = Enlightened One\n|title2           = Primus of the Order of the Deep\n|status           = Deceased\u003cbr\u003eSacrificed himself to drive back the [[Dark Tide]] beneath [[Ragunna]]'s sea.\u003cref\u003e{{Quest|Dawn Breaks on Dark Tides}}\u003c/ref\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- VAs --\u003e\n|voiceEN          = [[imdb:nm3899669| Rich Keeble]]\u003cref\u003eTwitter (X): [https://x.com/RichKeeble/status/1874751879328227796 EN VA Self Announcement]\u003c/ref\u003e \n|voiceCN          = Huang Yichuan ({{Lang|mini=1|zh=黄艺川}})\u003cref name=\"Carnevale Prologue Bilibili\u003eBilibili:[https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1uMk1YWEAd 《鸣潮》2.0动画短片 | 狂欢序章]\u003c/ref\u003e\n|voiceJP          = {{w|Hideo Ishikawa|Ishikawa Hideo ({{Lang|mini=1|ja=石川英郎}})}}\u003cref name=\"Carnevale Prologue Bilibili/\u003e\n|voiceKR          = [https://namu.wiki/w/정성훈(성우) Jeong Seong-hun ({{Lang|mini=1|ko=정성훈}})]\u003cref name=\"Carnevale Prologue Bilibili/\u003e\n|title3=Fenrico the First}}\n{{Description|{{A|Vo hrt rinascita interludes 406 15.ogg}} ''So, were I to choose anew, I would tread this path once more... though it spurns the wisdom of every Primus before me, though nothing but trials and terrors lie ahead.''|Fenrico, [[A Stranger in a Strange Land]]\n}}\n'''Fenrico''' {{Lang|zh=芬莱克·麦克白}} was a quest-exclusive NPC in {{Location|Ragunna}}, who made his first appearance as a hologram inside the [[Cathedral of Mercury]] during {{Quest|The Sacred Breeze So Often Breathes}}. He made his first true appearance in {{Quest|What Yesterday Wept, Today Doth Sing}}, after which he could be found standing in place of his hologram.\n\nHe served as the Primus of the [[Order of the Deep]], as well as the self-proclaimed Resonator of [[Sentinel]] [[Imperator]].\n\n==Physical Description==\nFenrico was a tall and slim middle-aged man with slicked white hair and light blue eyes, he wears in his right face the piece of a golden Venetian mask.\n\n==Clothing==\nFenrico wears a long white cloak with a golden-yellow collar and triangular dark brown stripes that holds a long navy blue cape printed with golden-yellow drawings. He also wears a round golden-yellow collar, his cloak is hold by a dark brown rope printed with golden-yellow drawings. As well a dark gray skirt, a navy blue bracelet in his right arm, a golden-yellow metallic halo in his back and white shoes with a dark gray sole and a golden-yellow stripe.\n\n==Profile==\nFenrico served as the latest Primus of the Order of the Deep, making him the de facto ruler of [[Ragunna]] for the last two decades.\n\n===History===\nHe was once a student in the Order's Seminary prior to its destruction, and a former classmate who went on to be a Privy Councilor describes Fenrico as speaking passionately about an ideal dream world during those years. However, shortly after Fenrico became the new Primus, the two bid farewell to the [[Pilgrim's Sail]] as it departed, and the Privy Councilor described his face as 'shrouded by a strange shadow.'\u003cref\u003e[[Former Privy Councilor's Notes]]\u003c/ref\u003e\n\nShortly after this, a shift had occurred in the Order, as Fenrico went to extreme extents to impose the ideal of Unity onto the city. Initially, the Pilgrim's Sail was discontinued, and the performances of the [[Carnevale]] were heavily restricted. Ten years after becoming Primus, Fenrico secretly sabotaged the Carnevale. Describing the tragedy as a divine punishment, he banned the Carnevale, and later reinstated the Pilgrim's Sail as punishment for those who violate doctrine, citing that the power of punishment and indoctrination shall be returned to the Sentinel.\n\nFenrico's former classmate lamented these changes and he, too, was ultimately sentenced by the Order Penitentiary, and noted that Fenrico was absent when he boarded the ship. He presumably lost his life at sea.\n\nAccording to Fenrico's own account of the events of two decades ago, during the martyrdom of the Blessed Maiden to the [[Dark Tide]], he discovered that [[Cartethyia|Fleurdelys]] had deceived everyone and was actually the [[Resonator]] of the [[Threnodian]]. Swearing himself to silence to keep the people from faltering, he accepted the Divinity's blessing and was granted new authority to cleanse the aftermath of the Dark Tide, becoming the new Enlightened One.\u003cref\u003e[[What Yesterday Wept, Today Doth Sing]]\u003c/ref\u003e\n\nFearing that public unrest might once again stir divisionist sentiments and summon the [[Dark Tide]], Fenrico decided to fashion himself as the Enlightened One, wielding divine authority to deliver oracles and placate the people. However, the relentless corrosion of Threnodian gradually blurred his features, leading him to henceforth conceal his face behind a mask. In collaboration with the Fractsidus, he constructed the Fabricatorium of the Deep beneath the Ragunna seabed, seeking to seize the Threnodian gemstone and achieve the Unity. \n\n===Current Day===\nLater, awakened by the lantern of the first Primus [[Napoli II]], he resolved to sacrifice himself to seal the Dark Tide.\u003cref\u003e[[Dreamcatchers in the Secret Gardens]]\u003c/ref\u003e This lantern, passed through the hands of [[Qiuyuan]], was eventually entrusted to the [[Rover]].\n\n==Quests and Events==\n{{Quests and Events}}\n\n==Gallery==\n===Videos===\n\u003cgallery\u003e\nWuthering Waves Version 2.0 Story Cinematics - Carnevale's Prologue-2\nWuthering Waves Version 2.5 Official Trailer - Unfading Melody of Life-2\n\u003c/gallery\u003e\n\n==Trivia==\n*Although described as a Resonator, his [[Forte]] was never revealed.\n\n===Etymology=== \n*Fenrico is very close to the Italian name Enrico, meaning \"home ruler\".\n*The surname Macbeth originates from Shakespeare's tragedy ''Macbeth'', with lines such as \"So foul and fair a day I have not seen.\" also quoted from the play.\n\n==Other Languages==\n{{Other Languages\n|en   = Fenrico Macbeth\n|zhs  = 芬莱克·麦克白\n|zht  = 芬萊克·麥克白\n|ja   = フェンリコ·マクベス\n|ko   = 펜리코 맥베스\n|es   = Fenrico Macbeth\n|fr   = Fenrico Macbeth\n|de   = Fenrico Macbeth\n}}\n\n==Change History==\n{{Change History|2.0}}\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n[[zh:芬莱克]]",
